2. The SGP4 verification element sets

Tests/GPKitTests/Resources/SGP4-VER.TLE is the set of verification cases published with the paper above. The copy
here is the one python-sgp4 distributes, unmodified:

    brandon-rhodes/python-sgp4, sgp4/SGP4-VER.TLE
    https://github.com/brandon-rhodes/python-sgp4
    commit 8126f773923c2902719d45aab8bdb5cce86cf39d
    SHA-256  d246d1d9d768ace445a38a965713fa9ba52d80fd8a41a0502ff83d7acffe2881

python-sgp4 is released under the MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2012-2016 Brandon Rhodes. The file is used by the tests
and is no part of the library.


3. The element sets and the reference of the pass comparison

Tests/GPKitTests/Resources/pass-check-sets.tle holds five element sets. Four are from the derived files of gpconf,
the GP/OMM conformance corpus (https://github.com/hneogy/gp-omm-conformance, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 NEOGY LLC),
at commit bec466b: the three of derived/corrupt-input/unedited-sets.tle and the one of
derived/alpha5-tle/alpha5-A-100000-saramago-first.tle. The fifth, 08195, is from the verification file above.

Tests/GPKitTests/Resources/skyfield-passes.json holds what Skyfield 1.55 (https://github.com/skyfielders/python-skyfield,
MIT, Copyright (c) 2013-2018 Brandon Rhodes) computes for those five: tools/skyfield_passes_reference.py wrote it.

Both are used by the tests and are no part of the library.
